IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ga-dates`

-- Guardianship Act 1987 (NSW) -- Part 1: the definitions every other Part turns on (ss 3(1), 3(2), 3D, 3E), from the
-- seat of the person the Act is applied to.
--
-- SEAT: the adult (or young person of 16 or 17) who has, or may be found to have, a disability: the person who appoints
-- an enduring guardian, the person about whom a guardianship or financial management order is sought or made, and the
-- patient on whom medical or dental treatment is proposed. Every exported question is one that person would ask ("Do I
-- count as having a disability?", "Who counts as my carer?").
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no question answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no (a "means" definition, a
-- condition introduced by "if", "unless" or "only if", a flat "is not"), or NOTHING where the Act does not answer on
-- the facts given; each NOTHING carries a "NOTHING-kind" comment. Judgments of the Tribunal and of others are asked as
-- facts, never decided.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025; version as at 27 March 2021; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Guardianship Act 1987 -- Part 1 definitions`

§§ `s 3(2) -- a person who has a disability`

-- s 3(2) "a reference to a person who has a disability is a reference to a person-- (a) who is intellectually,
-- physically, psychologically or sensorily disabled, (b) who is of advanced age, (c) who is a mentally ill person within
-- the meaning of the Mental Health Act 2007, or (d) who is otherwise disabled, and who, by virtue of that fact, is
-- restricted in one or more major life activities to such an extent that he or she requires supervision or social
-- habilitation." "Advanced age" and "mentally ill person" (a borrowed term) are asked as facts.
DECLARE `My condition` IS ONE OF
    `I am intellectually, physically, psychologically or sensorily disabled`
    `I am of advanced age`
    `I am a mentally ill person within the meaning of the Mental Health Act 2007`
    `I am otherwise disabled`
    `none of these`

GIVEN `my condition` IS A `My condition`
      `because of it I am restricted in a major life activity so that I need supervision or social habilitation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a person who has a disability` `my condition` `because of it I am restricted in a major life activity so that I need supervision or social habilitation` IF
    CONSIDER `my condition`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `because of it I am restricted in a major life activity so that I need supervision or social habilitation`

@export Do I count as a person who has a disability for the Guardianship Act (s 3(2))?
GIVEN `my condition` IS A `My condition` @desc Which describes you. One of: "I am intellectually, physically, psychologically or sensorily disabled", "I am of advanced age", "I am a mentally ill person within the meaning of the Mental Health Act 2007", "I am otherwise disabled", "none of these"
      `because of it I am restricted in a major life activity so that I need supervision or social habilitation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, because of that condition, you are restricted in one or more major life activities to such an extent that you need supervision or social habilitation (help to learn or keep everyday living skills)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Do I count as a person who has a disability` MEANS
    IF `a person who has a disability` `my condition` `because of it I am restricted in a major life activity so that I need supervision or social habilitation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- s 3(2) is a "means" definition ("is a reference to a person who ... and who ...")

§§ `s 3(1) -- a person in need of a guardian`

-- s 3(1) "person in need of a guardian means a person who, because of a disability, is totally or partially incapable of
-- managing his or her person." Capacity to manage one's person is asked as a fact (in proceedings it is for the Tribunal,
-- and s 6N lets a medical certificate be evidence of it).
DECLARE `How far I can manage my person` IS ONE OF
    `I am totally incapable of managing my person`
    `I am partially incapable of managing my person`
    `I am capable of managing my person`

GIVEN `my condition` IS A `My condition`
      `because of it I am restricted in a major life activity so that I need supervision or social habilitation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `how far I can manage my person` IS A `How far I can manage my person`
      `the incapacity is because of that disability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a person in need of a guardian` `my condition` `because of it I am restricted in a major life activity so that I need supervision or social habilitation` `how far I can manage my person` `the incapacity is because of that disability` IF
        `a person who has a disability` `my condition` `because of it I am restricted in a major life activity so that I need supervision or social habilitation`
    AND `the incapacity is because of that disability`
    AND (CONSIDER `how far I can manage my person`
         WHEN `I am capable of managing my person` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

@export Am I a person in need of a guardian: because of a disability, totally or partially incapable of managing my person (ss 3(1), 3(2))?
GIVEN `my condition` IS A `My condition` @desc Which describes you. One of: "I am intellectually, physically, psychologically or sensorily disabled", "I am of advanced age", "I am a mentally ill person within the meaning of the Mental Health Act 2007", "I am otherwise disabled", "none of these"
      `because of it I am restricted in a major life activity so that I need supervision or social habilitation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, because of that condition, you are restricted in one or more major life activities to such an extent that you need supervision or social habilitation
      `how far I can manage my person` IS A `How far I can manage my person` @desc How far you can manage your person (your own life, health and living arrangements, as distinct from money and property). One of: "I am totally incapable of managing my person", "I am partially incapable of managing my person", "I am capable of managing my person"
      `the incapacity is because of that disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any incapacity to manage your person is because of that disability
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I a person in need of a guardian` MEANS
    IF `a person in need of a guardian` `my condition` `because of it I am restricted in a major life activity so that I need supervision or social habilitation` `how far I can manage my person` `the incapacity is because of that disability`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- a "means" definition

§§ `s 3D -- who has the care of me`

-- s 3D(1) "the circumstances in which a person is to be regarded as having the care of another person include (but are
-- not limited to) the case where the person, otherwise than for remuneration (whether from the other person or any other
-- source), on a regular basis-- (a) provides domestic services and support to the other person, or (b) arranges for the
-- other person to be provided with such services and support." s 3D(3): remuneration does not include a carer's pension.
-- s 3D(2) "A person who resides in an institution (such as a hospital, nursing home, group home, boarding-house or
-- hostel) at which he or she is cared for by some other person is not, merely because of that fact, to be regarded as
-- being in the care of that other person, and remains in the care of the person in whose care he or she was immediately
-- before residing in the institution." The list in (1) is open ("include (but are not limited to)"): a case outside it is
-- NOTHING. The flat "is not ... to be regarded" in (2) is JUST FALSE.
GIVEN `they had my care immediately before I began living in an institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they regularly provide, or arrange, domestic services and support for me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are paid for it, other than by a carer's pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they care for me only as the institution I live in` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the person has the care of me` `they had my care immediately before I began living in an institution` `they regularly provide, or arrange, domestic services and support for me` `they are paid for it, other than by a carer's pension` `they care for me only as the institution I live in` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `they had my care immediately before I began living in an institution` THEN JUST TRUE  -- s 3D(2) "remains in the care of"
           IF `they care for me only as the institution I live in` THEN JUST FALSE  -- s 3D(2) flat "is not ... to be regarded"
           IF `they regularly provide, or arrange, domestic services and support for me` AND (NOT `they are paid for it, other than by a carer's pension`) THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (the s 3D(1) list "include[s] (but [is] not limited to)"; fork F2)

@export Does this person count as having the care of me (s 3D)?
GIVEN `they had my care immediately before I began living in an institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this person had your care immediately before you began living in an institution such as a hospital, nursing home, group home, boarding-house or hostel (answer no if you do not live in one)
      `they regularly provide, or arrange, domestic services and support for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this person, on a regular basis, provides domestic services and support to you, or arranges for you to be provided with them
      `they are paid for it, other than by a carer's pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this person is paid for that care (by you or anyone else); a carer's pension does not count as pay
      `they care for me only as the institution I live in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this person (or body) cares for you only because you live in their hospital, nursing home, group home, boarding-house or hostel
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does this person have the care of me` MEANS
    `the person has the care of me` `they had my care immediately before I began living in an institution` `they regularly provide, or arrange, domestic services and support for me` `they are paid for it, other than by a carer's pension` `they care for me only as the institution I live in`

§§ `s 3E -- a close friend or relative`

-- s 3E(1) "A person is a close friend or relative of another person for the purposes of this Act if the person
-- maintains both a close personal relationship with the other person through frequent personal contact and a personal
-- interest in the other person's welfare. However, a person is not to be regarded as a close friend or relative if the
-- person is receiving remuneration (whether from the other person or some other source) for, or has a financial interest
-- in, any services that he or she performs for the other person in relation to the person's care." s 3E(3): a carer's
-- pension is not remuneration. The "if" condition failing is JUST FALSE; the "However ... is not" is a flat negative.
-- Guidelines under s 3E(2) may say more; they are not deposited (fork F3).
GIVEN `frequent personal contact and a close personal relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a personal interest in my welfare` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paid for, or with a financial interest in, services they perform for my care` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a close friend or relative` `frequent personal contact and a close personal relationship` `a personal interest in my welfare` `paid for, or with a financial interest in, services they perform for my care` IF
        `frequent personal contact and a close personal relationship`
    AND `a personal interest in my welfare`
    AND (NOT `paid for, or with a financial interest in, services they perform for my care`)

@export Does this person count as my close friend or relative under the Act (s 3E)?
GIVEN `frequent personal contact and a close personal relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this person keeps up a close personal relationship with you through frequent personal contact
      `a personal interest in my welfare` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this person keeps up a personal interest in your welfare
      `paid for, or with a financial interest in, services they perform for my care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this person is paid (other than by a carer's pension), or has a financial interest in, any services they perform for you in relation to your care
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is this person my close friend or relative` MEANS
    IF `a close friend or relative` `frequent personal contact and a close personal relationship` `a personal interest in my welfare` `paid for, or with a financial interest in, services they perform for my care`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- "is ... if", and "However ... is not to be regarded"
